# 🏨 Residency-MERN — 3-Tier Architecture on Kubernetes

[Kubernetes](https://img.shields.io/badge/Kubernetes-326CE5?style=for-the-badge&logo=kubernetes&logoColor=white)
![React](https://img.shields.io/badge/React-61DAFB?style=for-the-badge&logo=react&logoColor=black)
![Node.js](https://img.shields.io/badge/Node.js-339933?style=for-the-badge&logo=nodedotjs&logoColor=white)
![MongoDB](https://img.shields.io/badge/MongoDB-47A248?style=for-the-badge&logo=mongodb&logoColor=white)
![Docker](https://img.shields.io/badge/Docker-2496ED?style=for-the-badge&logo=docker&logoColor=white)

> Full-stack hotel booking system deployed on Kubernetes (minikube)
> using a 3-tier architecture — React frontend, Node.js API backend
> and MongoDB database — each running as separate Kubernetes workloads.

---

## What is 3-Tier Architecture?

```
Tier 1 — Presentation  → React frontend (what users see)
Tier 2 — Application   → Node.js + Express API (business logic)
Tier 3 — Data          → MongoDB (stores all bookings)

Each tier runs independently in its own pod(s)
Each tier scales independently
Each tier has its own Kubernetes Service
```

---

## Architecture Diagram

```
Internet / Browser
        │
        ▼
┌─────────────────────────┐
│   Ingress (Nginx)       │  ← single entry point
│   hotel.local           │
└────────────┬────────────┘
             │
     ┌───────┴────────┐
     │                │
     ▼                ▼
/            →  /api/ →
┌──────────────┐  ┌──────────────────┐
│  TIER 1      │  │  TIER 2          │
│  Frontend    │  │  Backend API     │
│  React+Nginx │  │  Node.js+Express │
│  (2 replicas)│  │  (2 replicas)    │
└──────────────┘  └────────┬─────────┘
                           │
                           ▼
                  ┌──────────────────┐
                  │  TIER 3          │
                  │  MongoDB         │
                  │  (StatefulSet)   │
                  │  PersistentVolume│
                  └──────────────────┘
```

